{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q418860","formula":"C₅H₁₂O₁₁P₂","hill":"C5H12O11P2","elements":["H","C","O","P"],"composition":{"C":5.0,"H":12.0,"O":11.0,"P":2.0},"names":{"en":"D-ribulose 1,5-bisphosphate","ru":"Рибулозо-1,5-бисфосфат"},"descriptions":{"en":"Ribulose 1,5-bisphosphate (RuBP) is an organic substance that is involved in photosynthesis, notably as the principal CO2 acceptor in plants. It is a colourless anion, a double phosphate ester of the ketopentose (ketone-containing sugar with five carbon atoms) called ribulose. Salts of RuBP can be isolated, but its crucial biological function happens in solution.","ru":"Рибулозо-1,5-бисфосфат (рибулозо-1,5-дифосфат, РуБФ) — двойной сложный эфир пятичленного сахара рибулозы и фосфорной кислоты. В растворе присутствует в форме бесцветного аниона. Эта молекула выполняет важную биологическую функцию, она — главный акцептор CO2 в реакции фиксации углекислого газа."},"fame":22,"pubchemCid":123658,"mass":310.09,"charge":0,"smiles":"C([C@H]([C@H](C(=O)COP(=O)(O)O)O)O)OP(=O)(O)O","inchikey":"YAHZABJORDUQGO-NQXXGFSBSA-N","iupac":"[(2R,3R)-2,3-dihydroxy-4-oxo-5-phosphonooxypentyl] dihydrogen phosphate","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"123658","atoms":30,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":3.642,"y":1.469,"z":0.102,"el":"P"},{"x":-3.959,"y":1.116,"z":-0.088,"el":"P"},{"x":1.978,"y":-2.058,"z":-1.678,"el":"O"},{"x":2.694,"y":0.445,"z":-0.712,"el":"O"},{"x":0.757,"y":-3.025,"z":0.691,"el":"O"},{"x":-2.874,"y":0.116,"z":0.583,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.11,"y":-1.492,"z":1.782,"el":"O"},{"x":4.407,"y":0.521,"z":1.167,"el":"O"},{"x":2.585,"y":2.279,"z":1.019,"el":"O"},{"x":4.532,"y":2.327,"z":-0.748,"el":"O"},{"x":-4.648,"y":0.216,"z":-1.241,"el":"O"},{"x":-3.036,"y":2.148,"z":-0.924,"el":"O"},{"x":-4.91,"y":1.758,"z":0.879,"el